  "body": "## What changed\n\n**The default verdict is unchanged.** If the user does nothing, every non-fixture model is still judged as the part, exactly as before. A casting copied into a \"from model\" stock and left in the tree leaves the gouge verdict only when the user ticks **\"The source model is raw stock only (not judged as the part)\"** on the stock page (shown for a from-model stock).\n\nThe first push of this PR guessed which model was the part. The review reproduced a real 5 mm gouge posting with an empty gate (a stock made from the part itself, plus an unrelated model an op touches, live or suppressed). That guess is removed. The rule is now explicit:\n\n- `SetStockSourceOnly` (new, `crates/app/src/commands/stock_source_only.rs`): one undoable step on the active setup's stock. It is refused by name when the stock is not made from a model. It writes `schema::StockSourceOnly { source }` on the stock entity.\n- MCP `set_raw_stock_only { on }` (`crates/app/src/mcp/setup_tools.rs`) runs the same command.\n- UI: a checkbox under the stock page's Source picker (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/raw_stock_row.rs`), which queues `CommandKind::SetRawStockOnly`.\n- Project file: optional `raw_stock_only` on the stock row, absent = false. No version bump: an older reader drops the key and judges more, never less. An unmarked document saves as before.\n- `stock_source::stock_only_model`: the marked source leaves the verdict only while every stock the program starts from is a copy of that model and carries the mark. A new `SetStock` source drops the mark's hold. Any operation (any setup, suppressed included) that names the model in its source or in a boundary pick puts it back in the verdict.\n- `posting_sim`: when the mark leaves no other model, the post is refused by name (\"nothing is judged as the part: ...\"). A gouge refusal on the program stock's source adds one plain sentence pointing at the checkbox, or saying why the mark did not hold. That hint is the only inference left, and it changes no verdict.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1094-stock-source-not-part.md`. It covers the explicit rule (orchestrator's direction, taken unattended), the dropped inference and clause-by-clause patches, reader-side vs refusing the mark, and refuse vs warn.\n\n## Other readers of \"every non-fixture model\"\n\n| Reader | Changed? | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `simulate_document`, carry `judge`, field view, judged playback | yes, only when marked | all read `part_facets` / `parts_facets_in` |\n| model-excess law `model_fidelity::verdict_tol` (#864/#911) | no | a coarse casting still tightens or refuses the verdict: a false refusal at worst |\n| per-op collision / rapid / cross-drill laws | no | read the op's own source or the stock, not the document part set |\n| rest material | no | reads the stock walk |\n| alignment, picks, fixture clash, tree, GPU list | no | placement and display, not judgement |\n\n## Tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/stock_source_verdict.rs` (11, all pass):\n- `a_stock_made_from_the_part_with_an_unrelated_model_beside_it_refuses_the_gouge`: the review's reproduction 1, which must refuse (default).\n- `the_same_with_the_unrelated_op_suppressed_still_refuses`: the review's reproduction 2.\n- `marked_an_op_naming_the_model_puts_it_back_in_the_verdict`: marked, plus an op (suppressed) naming the part. The gouge still blocks, and the hint says why.\n- `marked_a_boundary_pick_on_the_model_puts_it_back_in_the_verdict`: the review's item 3.\n- `unmarked_the_casting_is_judged_and_the_refusal_says_how_to_mark_it`: the issue's job, off. It refuses, with the hint.\n- `marked_raw_stock_only_the_casting_leaves_the_verdict_and_the_program_posts`: the issue's job, on. It posts.\n- `marked_the_separate_part_stays_judged_a_cut_below_its_floor_blocks`\n- `a_mark_that_leaves_nothing_to_judge_refuses_by_name`\n- `the_mark_undoes_redoes_and_a_new_stock_source_drops_its_hold`\n- `the_mark_is_refused_on_a_stock_not_made_from_a_model`\n- `the_mark_round_trips_the_project_file_and_an_older_file_judges_as_before`\n\nOther new tests:\n- `mcp_setup::set_raw_stock_only_marks_the_stock_source_through_the_command`: same command, undo, refusals.\n- ui `egui_app::tests::raw_stock_row::the_stock_page_ticks_raw_stock_only_through_the_command_and_undo`: AccessKit label click, undo. Structural, no PNG.\n\nSuites green: `edge_break_gate` (5), `solid_law_goldens` (1), `stock_sim_document` (9), `operations` (117, 6 ignored), `golden_cl` (25), `project_roundtrip` (71), `post_not_judged` (4), `mcp` (13), `mcp_setup` (7). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green - app suites + ui suites, 0 failed (10.4 min).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Multi-setup documents (aligned, or carried with \"what the setup before leaves\") with a marked casting. The rule reads them, but no test drives a spanned program.\n- The GUI was not launched. The checkbox is proven by the kittest harness only.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill's tool table (`.claude/skills/`, a process file) does not list `set_raw_stock_only` yet. Left out so this PR needs no `PROCESS_VERSION` bump.\n- #1091's `stepped_stock_rapid.rs` still deletes its casting as a workaround. With this PR it could tick the mark instead (not touched here).\n\nChangelog: A stock made from a model gets a \"The source model is raw stock only (not judged as the part)\" setting (stock page, MCP `set_raw_stock_only`, saved in the project). Ticked, a casting left in the tree is no longer judged as the finished part, so a legal program over a separate part posts. Off by default, so nothing changes until the user ticks it. A gouge on the stock's source now says where the setting is. (#1094)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation; reworked after review)\n\nFixes #1094\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
